A||||8||Galen||Ideals of a Southern Man Part 6||||3||
Z||000000||Galen||09-08-2001||01:03 AM||||Okey I know, I know, Not many of you have read my previous posts on this very subject. But I am at part six. This is merely my rant, I do not aim to offend. But in the event I do offend someone, due to some possible slip of my finger. I do say this, I am sorry that I offended you, however I am not sorry for my ideals or my views. They are my and mine alone and may or may not reflect the views of others on this board. <P>Now with that rather long little jumble of words out of the way, lets get to what I wanted to say. 4 years ago, back in August of '97, yes way back then, I was nearing the end of my 3 years of using bulletin boards and got introduced to the net through a friend I met on one of those bbs's. I didn't know about tcp/ip stuff so I merely dialed in the same way I would a bbs. I telenetted to another bbs hehe and found myself quickly bored of the board. Hardly any games, hardly any msg boards, useless trash. <P>But then, I wanted somewhere and found IRC, Internet Relay chat. I was joined to a channel called #WorldGroup on IRCnet. Which, yes, I do still visit. I was a cocky lil newbie, as most I have learned now are. I talked junk to everyone and I was quickly kicked rather frequently. I came back and would get kicked, and I'd come back again. Slowly making some friends there. Then I got banned. Was rather funny now that I think back to it, But at the time it pissed me off. I figured I'd make em pay, Didn't know how but I would.  I went and started my own channel and started taking users from their channel to mine. That failed. <P>Then I found out about TCP/IP, windows networking, and mIRC  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Wonderful mIRC, still visited the same channel. I calmed myself back some and started making friends rather quickly. Alot of those to this day I still consider a friend.<P>What am I trying to convey here? I dont know, Am I trying to convey something? doubtful. But this knowledge has stuck in my head, friends do not have to be flesh and blood touchable to be friends(I'm not condoning play with your friends blood), merely reachable.. in a sense of mind togetherness. <P>One friend I met was from England, he recently moved to the US to get married to his wife who lives in Ohio. He told me after he got married, that I was one of the best friends he'd ever had. That he'd do anything he could for me if I needed him to. Thinking back to it now, it proves my before mentioned point.<P>Friends are not psychical, They are not a 'body'.. Friends are those connections with people that are made. <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Sorry if this was a non-ending, pointless rant. I just notice all too often people badmouthing 'meeting friends on the net'... Your thoughts?<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||3
Z||000001||maryjane||09-08-2001||01:11 AM||||I 'think' I know what you mean, I've got friends on the net myself, that I probably will never meet. Hopefully, I will but it is doubtfull for a lot of them. That doesn't mean I care less just because they are a half a country or world away. It's funny how you can meet people on the web and seem to know them. He**, they could all be axe murderers for all I know. I imagine a lot more people read your"Ideals" than you think. Don't always follow them, but this time I think I do.<BR>Don||||reg||1
