Z||000007||fierobaby||09-08-2001||10:18 PM||||Galen you are so right! :-) hehehe<P>I have a great friend named Chris he live in Georgia... pretty far..will most likely never meet him but I still concider him one of my best friends I can tell him anything. I think you're right about Friends not being a body but a connection. I believe on-line friends are sometimes better than real life friends although I like both! <P>I met Scott online orignally. I am extreamly happy that I gave him a chance...HE actually came over one night... my parents were here and everything... they had no problem with me meeting someone from online as long as it is at my house or a public place.. I have met some wounderful people in real life from online.. like Keith. he and I still talk almost every single day.<P>Corinne<P>[edited to add more]<p>[This message has been edited by fierobaby (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||09-08-2001||10:26 PM||||another thing. several friends I made online, I have since met up with in person.. sure there's the occasional nut, (same as anywhere else..) but I've found the net a pretty good place to meet people with similar interests, ie. Fieros<P>I have a friend whom I used to play Quake with online, back in late 1996.. I still talk with him almost every day on icq, he's a good friend, even though we've never met in person. I've also met a few girls online, but that never turned out so well.. heh<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
